 will always be a valid solution, and any correct answer is acceptable. For example, if  \"bcbc\", we can either remove 'b' at index  or 'c' at index .  Input Format  The first line contains an integer, , denoting the number of test cases.  Each line  of the  subsequent lines (where ) describes a test case in the form of a single string, .  Constraints  All characters are lowercase English letters. Output Format  Print an integer denoting the zero-indexed position of the character that makes  not a palindrome; if  is already a palindrome or no such character exists, print .  Sample Input  3 aaab baa aaa Sample Output  3 0 -1 Explanation  Test Case 1: \"aaab\"  Removing 'b' at index  results in a palindrome, so we print  on a new line.  Test Case 2: \"baa\"  Removing 'b' at index  results in a palindrome, so we print  on a new line.  Test Case 3: \"aaa\"  This string is already a palindrome, so we print ; however, , , and  are also all acceptable answers, as the string will still be a palindrome if any one of the characters at those indices are removed.","topics":[],"score":2299,"global_rank":136221},{"name":"guillaumethomas/LeanKit","owner":"guillaumethomas","html_url":"https://github.com/guillaumethomas/LeanKit","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2299,"global_rank":136227},{"name":"brady800526/Practice-Blockchain-Snakecoin_Python","owner":"brady800526","html_url":"https://github.com/brady800526/Practice-Blockchain-Snakecoin_Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2299,"global_rank":136228},{"name":"saugatt/traceroute-project","owner":"saugatt","html_url":"https://github.com/saugatt/traceroute-project","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2299,"global_rank":136235},{"name":"jSith/GroupBot","owner":"jSith","html_url":"https://github.com/jSith/GroupBot","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":5,"language":"Python","description":"Groupme Bots","topics":[],"score":2299,"global_rank":136237},{"name":"saransh2405/bi-gram-word-suggestion","owner":"saransh2405","html_url":"https://github.com/saransh2405/bi-gram-word-suggestion","stars":1,"forks":1,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"In the fields of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":2299,"global_rank":136241},{"name":"milton0825/cpython-internals","owner":"milton0825","html_url":"https://github.com/milton0825/cpython-internals","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2299,"global_rank":136243},{"name":"ipl-uw/Infant-Pose-Classification","owner":"ipl-uw","html_url":"https://github.com/ipl-uw/Infant-Pose-Classification","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":2,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2299,"global_rank":136254},{"name":"RAnderso0325/dog-image-classifier","owner":"RAnderso0325","html_url":"https://github.com/RAnderso0325/dog-image-classifier","stars":0,"forks":2,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2299,"global_rank":136259},{"name":"yangchris11/MOTRv2","owner":"yangchris11","html_url":"https://github.com/yangchris11/MOTRv2","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":2299,"global_ran